## Working conventions

Read and follow [STYLE.md](STYLE.md) before changing Python code or tests.
`pyproject.toml` is the source of truth for dependency groups, Ruff, mypy,
pytest, and coverage configuration.

Keep changes focused, preserve public behavior unless the task intentionally
changes it, and add or update tests for behavior changes.

{% if changelog -%}
Changelog fragments are added only when merging into `{{ integration_branch }}`.
Review the incoming branch's commit messages and Git history not yet in
`{{ integration_branch }}` (for example, `git log {{ integration_branch }}..SOURCE`)
and write fragments describing its user-visible changes.
Do not add or update fragments for individual changes or commits, or for merges
into other branches. Towncrier assembles the fragments during release preparation.
{% else -%}
This project does not use a changelog or Towncrier.
{% endif %}
## Development notes

Use `wiki/` to record concise, durable development context.
Read [wiki/example.md](wiki/example.md) before starting a note, and
replace it with notes that capture decisions, validation results, and useful
follow-up work.

## Validation

{% if tasks == "nox" -%}
Use direct pytest for a focused run and the generated Nox script for checks:

```console
uv run noxfile.py -s lint
uv run noxfile.py -s typecheck
uv run pytest
```

Use `uv run noxfile.py -s tests` for the full supported-Python matrix.
{%- else -%}
Run the appropriate dependency group directly:

```console
uv run --group lint pre-commit run --all-files
uv run --group type mypy {{ package_path }} tests scripts
uv run --group test pytest
```
{%- endif -%}
